# Environment for the UNIT test tier (`pnpm test`).
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS FAKE AND THIS FILE IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. Do not put a
# real credential in it — `.gitignore` covers `.env`, not `.env.test`, so a real
# secret pasted here goes straight into the repo. If you need real values, they
# belong in `.env` (ignored) and the integration tier reads those instead.
#
# WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST AT ALL
# lib/env.ts validates the whole environment at import time and calls
# process.exit(1) when it doesn't parse. Importing createApp() therefore
# transitively requires these three variables to be *present and well-formed*,
# even for tests that never open a socket to any of them. Node's --env-file
# loads this before the first import; process.env still wins on conflict, so a
# real value already exported in the shell is not clobbered.
#
# Deliberately UNSET below: REDIS_URL. lib/redis.ts exports `null` when it is
# missing, which means no client, no connection, and no open handle keeping the
# test runner's event loop alive after the last assertion.

# Must parse as a URL (z.url()). Nothing connects to it in this tier — the pg
# Pool is lazy, so a query is what would fail, and unit tests never issue one.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/test_never_connected"

# Must be >= 32 characters. Real tokens are signed and verified with this during
# the tests, which is fine: the key is fake, so the tokens are worthless.
JWT_SECRET="test-secret-not-used-anywhere-real-0123456789"

# Must be non-empty. No request is ever made with it in this tier.
OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-fake-openai-key-for-unit-tests-only"

# Switches rate limiters off (see middleware/rate-limit.ts `skip`). Without it a
# test would pass or fail depending on how many tests ran before it.
NODE_ENV="test"
